# CAR (theta0 = 0) with CRVAL2 = 0 and LONPOLE = 90: |phip - phi0| = 90,
# so celset's z = sqrt((cos theta0 cos(phip - phi0))^2 + sin^2 theta0) is
# exactly 0 and the native-pole latitude is set by LATPOLE alone
# (latpreq = 2). LATPOLE = 95 is outside [-90, 90]; wcslib clamps it to
# latp = +90 and accepts the header. Twin: celpole_z0_latpolem95.
# Synthetic.
NOTE pipeline: celset z = 0 branch, LATPOLE > 90 clamped to 90
GRID 1 512 5 1 512 5
SKYGRID 0 350 8 -80 80 5
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 512
NAXIS2  = 512
CTYPE1  = 'RA---CAR'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--CAR'
CRVAL1  = 10.0
CRVAL2  = 0.0
CRPIX1  = 256.5
CRPIX2  = 256.5
CDELT1  = -0.1
CDELT2  = 0.1
LONPOLE = 90.0
LATPOLE = 95.0
